---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Terms of Use: Entertainment Purpose, No Medical or Psychological Diagnosis';
const description =
  'Terms of use for Which Deadly Sin: the quiz is for entertainment and reflection only, does not provide diagnosis, and is provided without warranty.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/terms/"
  type="article"
  publishedTime="2026-11-19"
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Terms', path: '/terms/' },
    ]}
  />

  <article class="prose-article mt-4">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 19 November 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing whichdeadlysins.com (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;) you agree to these terms. If you do
      not agree, please do not use the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Entertainment and reflection only</h2>
    <p>
      The quiz, results, and articles on the Site are provided for entertainment, education, and
      personal reflection only. They are <strong>not</strong> medical, psychological, psychiatric,
      or diagnostic services, are not validated clinical assessments, and must not be used as a
      substitute for professional advice. Never disregard professional guidance or delay seeking
      help because of something you read on this Site. If you are in crisis, contact local
      emergency services or a crisis support line in your country.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The Site and its content are provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; without warranties of any kind,
      whether express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or
      uninterrupted availability. Quiz results reflect your self-reported answers through a simple
      scoring formula and may be incomplete, inaccurate, or unsuitable for any specific decision.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Site and its operators are not liable for any
      direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from use of the Site or
      reliance on its content, including decisions about relationships, employment, health, or
      legal matters.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Site&rsquo;s text, quizzes, graphics, and generated share images are protected by
      applicable copyright laws. You may share short excerpts with attribution and a link, and you
      may share your personal quiz result. Republishing whole articles or mechanically copying the
      question set requires written permission via{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Do not attempt to disrupt the Site, probe its infrastructure, bypass security measures, or
      use automated systems to scrape content at a scale that degrades service for others. The quiz
      requires no registration, so any form of fake-account automation is also unnecessary.
    </p>

    <h2>7. External links</h2>
    <p>
      The Site may link to third-party websites for reference. We do not control and are not
      responsible for the content, privacy practices, or availability of those sites.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes and termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms or modify or discontinue any feature of the Site at any time.
      Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
    <!-- TODO: 上线前与运营主体确认适用法域后替换 -->
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws applicable to the operating entity of the Site, without
      regard to conflict-of-law rules. Any disputes will be resolved in the competent courts of
      that jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can be sent to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
